\bluebigheading{PROPOSAL DESCRIPTION}

\vspace{12mm}

\blueheading{Motivation }

\vspace{1mm}

\answerbox[5cm]{
Examination related works are handled through seating-plan documents and common lists. The seating arrangement along with other room details are shared in from of lists, thus the students have to search for their roll number to find out their respective room and seat.

For teachers, the examination duties are generally intimated through a common duty list. In case of any UFM (Unfair Means) case during an examination, the details are manually noted down on paper for further checking by the concerned authorities.

Although the current system handles all these works, finding out individual information from common lists might take time and be tedious. The goal of our project is to make the process easier, more organized and personalized by providing the user with all the information that concerns him/her through a common portal.
}

\vspace{12mm}

\blueheading{State of the Art / Current solution }

\vspace{1mm}

\answerbox[6.5cm]{
Currently, the students need to refer to the common seating list to find their seating details.It can take a long time to get the required information including building, floor, classroom and seat numbers which could also be confusing.


For the administrative personnel, the process commences by getting the student and room information and coming up with a tentative seating plan.



Any changes to the student’s information, the room or its availability, or the exam schedules would necessitate taking up the entire process again.



While the current system works well to provide the required seating information, it can be seen that as the number of students and rooms increases the process of allocating them becomes tedious and requires several checks and balances.



This shows the need of having an intelligent seating allocation system that can handle the seating arrangements and their amendments in a much more systematic and automated manner while eliminating the human errors that are involved in the current systems.
}

\vspace{12mm}

\blueheading{Project Goals and Milestones}

\vspace{1mm}

\answerbox[7cm]{
\noindent Project Goals
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=2.5em,label=$\bullet$,itemsep=0pt,parsep=0pt,topsep=0pt,partopsep=0pt]
\item To design an intelligent system for allocating seats which reduces the scope of error.
\item Allow students to fetch the details of their allotted seat easily by inputting their university roll number.
\item Display building, floor, room and seat information through the portal.
\item Provide teacher specific invigilation duties.
\item Manage UFM records digitally.
\item Apply DSA concepts to seating allocation and data management.
\end{itemize}

\vspace{1mm}

\noindent Milestones
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=2.5em,label=$\bullet$,itemsep=0pt,parsep=0pt,topsep=0pt,partopsep=0pt]
\item Data collection, Database and detailed analysis of the collected data.
\item Seating allocation algorithm.
\item Creating separate modules for students and teachers.
\item Admin module and UFM management.
\item Integration and testing.
\end{itemize}
}

